note: The window module: open a window, draw in it, read the keys and the mouse.
note: A program uses it with the line  import window  at the top.
note:
note: This file says what the module offers. The Plain compiler reads it, so the sentences below
note: are exactly the sentences you can write. window.py is the Python code that does the work.
note:
note: Each line has the form:   command|question  <sentence>  [gives <type>]  =  <function in window.py>
note: Words are written as they are. <name: type = example> is a value you fill in. The types are text,
note: number, boolean and color (a color name, a Color value, or three numbers).

module window
python window.py

note: A color you make yourself:  let sky be Color(red: 20, green: 24, blue: 40)
type Color
    red as number
    green as number
    blue as number
end

note: The color names. Red, green and blue go from 0 to 255.
colors
    red 230 50 50
    green 50 180 70
    blue 50 100 230
    yellow 250 220 50
    orange 255 150 30
    purple 150 70 200
    pink 255 130 180
    brown 140 90 50
    gray 128 128 128
    white 255 255 255
    black 0 0 0
end

note: Opening and closing
command open window <title: text = "My game"> with width <width: number = 640> and height <height: number = 480> = window_open
command close window = window_close
command show window = window_show
question window is open gives boolean = window_is_open

note: Colors
command use color <color: color = orange> = window_color
command clear window = window_clear
command clear window with color <color: color = black> = window_clear_with

note: Drawing. (0, 0) is the top left corner, x grows to the right and y grows downwards.
command draw rectangle at <x: number = 10>, <y: number = 10> size <width: number = 100> by <height: number = 50> = window_rectangle
command draw circle at <x: number = 200>, <y: number = 150> radius <radius: number = 30> = window_circle
command draw line from <x1: number = 0>, <y1: number = 0> to <x2: number = 100>, <y2: number = 100> = window_line
command draw text <text: text = "Score: 3"> at <x: number = 10>, <y: number = 10> = window_text

note: Keys and mouse
question key <name: text = "left"> is pressed gives boolean = window_key_pressed
question mouse x gives number = window_mouse_x
question mouse y gives number = window_mouse_y
question mouse is down gives boolean = window_mouse_down
